Z||000026||Patrick's Dad||12-08-2001||05:18 PM||||The solar projection method is not completely foolproof if you have a closed optical assembly (like a binocular or refractor telescope). Heat buildup inside the tube will eventually degrade the image, then the glass itself.<P>I just used a Baader Astrosolar Film solar filter on my C-5, and observed for a little over an hour. I just take care of it, and check it visually before each use.<P>A newtonian reflector can be used for projection without too much worry.||||reg||1
